<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The Argon2id password hashing surface targets all three LTS/STS lines.
         The PostQuantum.Jwt hybrid-token integration is net10.0-only because the
         BCL post-quantum primitives (ML-DSA/ML-KEM) and PostQuantum.Jwt itself
         ship for .NET 10. That code is gated behind #if NET10_0_OR_GREATER and a
         conditional package reference — see Tokens/ and KNOWN-GAPS.md. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>PostQuantum.Identity</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>PostQuantum.Identity</AssemblyName>
    <!-- The net10 token surface serializes claims via source-generated
         JsonTypeInfo<T> (PostQuantumIdentityJsonContext) and PostQuantum.Jwt's
         typed WithClaim<T> overload, so it is trim/AOT-clean. The Argon2id path
         (Konscious + Identity.Core) raises no trim warnings for our usage either.
         Asserted on net10 only — the trim/AOT analyzers ship with that SDK band. -->
    <IsAotCompatible Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet package metadata -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>PostQuantum.Identity</PackageId>
    <Version>0.3.0-preview.1</Version>
    <Title>PostQuantum.Identity — post-quantum ASP.NET Core Identity</Title>
    <Authors>Paul Clark</Authors>
    <Description>Post-quantum integration for ASP.NET Core Identity. Replaces the default PBKDF2 password hasher with Argon2id (PHC-formatted, secure-by-default work factors, transparent rehash-on-login, one-line PBKDF2→Argon2id migration) and issues post-quantum hybrid JWTs for authenticated users via PostQuantum.Jwt — ML-DSA-65 signatures (FIPS 204) with optional X-Wing (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) encryption. Drops into the standard Identity builder chain (AddArgon2idPasswordHasher / AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration / AddPostQuantumTokens). Argon2id hashing runs on net8.0/net9.0/net10.0; the hybrid-token integration requires .NET 10. Pinned to spec with RFC 9106 §5.3 Known Answer Tests + reference-CLI PHC interop + sign-then-encrypt envelope KATs. Ships with a CycloneDX SBOM, GitHub build-provenance attestation, deterministic SourceLink builds, and CodeQL coverage. Preview release — not independently audited, not for production use. See https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity for migration guide and runnable samples.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>aspnetcore;identity;aspnet-identity;password-hashing;argon2;argon2id;phc;owasp;jwt;jwt-token;post-quantum;pqc;quantum-resistant;ml-dsa;ml-kem;x-wing;hybrid-cryptography;authentication;cryptography;security;fips-204;sbom;cyclonedx;net8;net9;net10</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
0.3.0-preview.1 — Polish + assurance release. No public API changes from 0.2.

Cryptographic assurance:
  - Argon2id KATs hardened: RFC 9106 §5.3 reference vector (incl. keyed + AD path),
    canonical reference-`argon2`-CLI PHC string verification, wire-format pin of the
    PHC emitter, and compute-then-format-then-verify roundtrips across the OWASP
    2024 minimum / library default / stronger profile / documented minimum.
  - Token Known Answer Tests added: JOSE header pinning (typ:JWT, alg:ML-DSA-65,
    kid), registered-claim shape + timestamp consistency, single vs. multi-role
    array shape, sign-then-encrypt envelope (5-seg JWE, alg:X-Wing, enc:A256GCM,
    cty:JWT) with full validation roundtrip, and end-to-end recovered-claim
    equality.

Migration story:
  - `docs/MIGRATION.md` rewritten as a step-by-step transparent-migration guide
    with a PBKDF2 path, a bcrypt/scrypt path, work-factor tuning, a rollback
    section, and an FAQ. One-line registration via
    AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration.

Reference samples elevated:
  - PostQuantum.Identity.Demo (minimal API): adds /refresh (with old-jti
    revocation), /logout, /.well-known/pq-jwks key discovery, in-memory
    revocation middleware, ProblemDetails error responses, and per-endpoint
    walkthrough docs.
  - PostQuantum.Identity.Mvc.Demo (controllers): same elevated flows expressed
    with attribute routing.

Docs and supply chain:
  - README adds "When to use this library", a Comparison table vs. default
    Identity / Argon2id-alone / hand-rolled PQ JWT, and a Supply chain section
    with verification commands (SBOM + gh attestation).
  - SECURITY.md / KNOWN-GAPS.md refreshed with the expanded KAT corpus, the
    revocation contract, and the honest-statement updates.

Still preview — NOT independently audited, NOT for production use. See
KNOWN-GAPS.md.

Earlier: 0.2.0 added MigratingPasswordHasher (PBKDF2→Argon2id), kid rotation,
AOT-clean claim path, embedded CycloneDX SBOM, CI/release workflows, benchmarks.
0.1.0 was the initial Argon2id hasher + hybrid-token service.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Paul Clark</Copyright>
    <NeutralLanguage>en-US</NeutralLanguage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Symbols + SourceLink for debuggable, reproducible packages. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Argon2id implementation (Argon2 1.3 spec, PHC winner). Used on every TFM. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Konscious.Security.Cryptography.Argon2" Version="1.3.1" />
    <!-- Framework-agnostic ASP.NET Core Identity core: IPasswordHasher<TUser>,
         PasswordHasher<TUser>, IdentityBuilder, UserManager<TUser>. No EF / web host pulled in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Core" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Hybrid-token integration: PostQuantum.Jwt + BCL PQC ship for .NET 10 only. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="PostQuantum.Jwt" Version="1.0.0-preview.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Generate a CycloneDX SBOM (bom.json) inside the package on every Pack.
       Requires the `dotnet-CycloneDX` global tool (one-time install via
       `dotnet tool install` with the `global` flag and id `CycloneDX`). If the
       tool isn't present (e.g. a fresh dev machine), pack continues without the
       SBOM rather than failing; the release workflow installs the tool
       unconditionally, so CI always produces the SBOM.

       The bom.json is added via an in-target ItemGroup because
       $(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json doesn't exist when a static <None Include>
       would be evaluated. Pinned to the net10.0 graph so the tool runs once. -->
  <Target Name="GenerateCycloneDxSbom"
          BeforeTargets="GenerateNuspec;_GetPackageFiles"
          Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false' and '$(SbomDisabled)' != 'true'">
    <!-- IMPORTANT: the disable-package-restore flag is required. CycloneDX
         otherwise runs its own restore, and on a multi-targeted project that
         rewrites obj/project.assets.json to a single TFM, which then collapses
         the per-TFM dependency groups in the generated .nuspec (NU5128) and would
         drop transitive deps for net8.0/net9.0 consumers. With restore disabled
         it reads the existing multi-TFM assets and aggregates all frameworks. -->
    <Exec Command="dotnet CycloneDX &quot;$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)&quot; --disable-package-restore --output &quot;$(IntermediateOutputPath.TrimEnd('\').TrimEnd('/'))&quot; --filename bom.json --json"
          IgnoreExitCode="true"
          ContinueOnError="WarnAndContinue">
      <Output TaskParameter="ExitCode" PropertyName="_CycloneDxExitCode" />
    </Exec>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM not generated (tool missing or failed, exit=$(_CycloneDxExitCode)). Install with: `dotnet tool install` (global, id=CycloneDX)."
             Condition="'$(_CycloneDxExitCode)' != '0'" />
    <ItemGroup Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')">
      <None Include="$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM packed into .nupkg at /bom.json"
             Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')" />
  </Target>

</Project>
